# Project
Private members-only bilingual (English + Tamil) web app for the "Vada" O/L 1995 / A/L 1998 old students of 13 Vadamarachchi schools. Domain: vada9598.online. Hosted on AWS EC2 Linux.
Full spec: @BLUEPRINT.md. Progress and decisions: @AGENT.md. Read both before any task.

# Stack (do not change without asking)
Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript (strict) · Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui · Framer Motion · React Three Fiber + @react-three/drei · canvas-confetti · next-intl (member area only: en, ta) · Auth.js · PostgreSQL + Prisma · Zod · AWS S3 (media) · Amazon SES (email) · Recharts · Docker Compose + Nginx + Let's Encrypt on EC2 · GitHub Actions.

# Roles
MEMBER, ADMIN, SUPER_ADMIN. Super Admin: Mayooran. Admins: Mugunthan, Ramanan.

# Non-negotiable rules
1. Enforce role checks on the server in every route handler, server action and page. Never rely only on hiding UI.
2. Enforce per-field visibility (All members / Admins only) in the data layer. Hidden fields must never reach member API responses.
3. Every profile view writes exactly one ActivityLog row (VIEW_PROFILE, actorId, targetUserId, ip, userAgent, createdAt).
4. Consent is mandatory before a profile is visible. Store type, notice version, timestamp and IP.
4a. No Google Form and no CSV import. Members join only through the member details form on the public home page (/), which saves directly to PostgreSQL with status PENDING.
4b. Member details are editable by ADMIN / SUPER_ADMIN only. There is no member-facing edit form; server actions and APIs reject MemberProfile writes from MEMBER. Members get a read-only profile + "Request a change" (ChangeRequest) and can change only their password and language.
5. Member UI is EN + TA via next-intl; no hard-coded member-facing strings. The admin panel (/admin) is English only.
6. Identity No. format is VADA-001 (zero-padded), assigned in a DB transaction on approval. Never reuse a number.
7. Store all times in UTC and display them in the viewer's time zone. Birthdays: use the viewer's local date; 29 Feb is shown on 28 Feb in non-leap years.
8. Deceased members: status DECEASED, excluded from birthdays, profile read-only.
9. Write every Admin/Super Admin change to AuditLog. 2FA is required for ADMIN and SUPER_ADMIN.
10. Validate all input with Zod on the server. Validate uploads (type and size); keep media private and serve it via signed URLs.
11. Never commit secrets. Use .env with a .env.example.

# UI / 3D design ("Vada Reunion — Navy & Gold")
- Navy gradient #0B1530 → #13244D, gold #D4A84B, teal #2EC4B6, soft white text. Dark mode by default.
- Glassmorphism cards (backdrop-blur, light border, soft glow), layered depth, 16–24px radius, 44px+ touch targets, mobile-first, bottom nav on phones.
- Fonts: Inter/Poppins (EN), Noto Sans Tamil (TA, line-height ≥ 1.7).
- 3D: React Three Fiber scenes loaded with next/dynamic (ssr:false) and lazy-loaded; CSS 3D transforms for tilt and flip.
- Always respect prefers-reduced-motion and provide a fallback when WebGL is unavailable. 3D is an enhancement only; every feature must work without it.
- Performance: DPR ≤ 1.5, low-poly, pause rendering off-screen; Lighthouse mobile performance ≥ 85.
- Obituaries and In Memoriam are always calm: no 3D, tilt, confetti or bright color. Use muted grey/white, a soft glow and serif headings.
- Admin panel: mostly flat, fast, tables + Recharts.

# Way of working
- Do one task at a time. Before writing code, briefly list the files you will create or change.
- Keep scope to the current phase in AGENT.md. Ask before adding features not in BLUEPRINT.md.
- Write typed, commented, production-quality code. No placeholder logic unless marked TODO.
- After each task: run `npm run lint`, `npx tsc --noEmit` and the relevant tests, and fix errors.
- At the end of every task, update AGENT.md: tick the checklist, add to the Decisions log and Session log, and write the next step.
